    "# Introduction\n",
    "\n",
    "**Numerical Analysis** is a branch of mathematics and computer science that develops and studies algorithms for obtaining approximate solutions to mathematical problems that are difficult or impossible to solve exactly. Many real-world problems involve equations, integrals, differential equations, and large systems of calculations that cannot be solved analytically. Numerical analysis provides practical methods to obtain solutions with acceptable accuracy.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Why Numerical Analysis Is Important\n",
    "\n",
    "Many scientific and engineering problems involve:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Weather prediction\n",
    "* Aircraft design\n",
    "* Machine learning\n",
    "* Structural engineering\n",
    "* Financial modeling\n",
    "* Computer graphics\n",
    "* Physics simulations\n",
    "\n",
    "These problems often require approximations because exact solutions are either unavailable or too expensive to compute.\n",
    "\n",
    "For example:\n",
    "\n",
    "Find the root of:\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x^3-x-2=0\n",
    "$$\n",
    "This equation has no simple exact algebraic solution, so numerical methods are used to approximate the root.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Main Areas of Numerical Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "### Root Finding\n",
    "\n",
    "Finding values of x that satisfy:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "f(x)=0\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "**Common Methods**\n",
    "\n",
    "* [Bisection Method](#Bisection-Method)\n",
    "* [Newton-Raphson Method](##Newton-Raphson-Method)\n",
    "* [Secant Method](#Secant-Method)\n",
    "* Fixed Point Iteration\n",
    "* [False Position Method](#False-Position-Method)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Example**\n",
    "\n",
    "Solve:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x^2-4=0\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Exact roots:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x=2,-2\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Using numerical methods, we can approximate the roots even if exact solutions are unknown.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Numerical Linear Algebra\n",
    "\n",
    "Deals with solving systems of equations:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "Ax=b\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\begin{aligned}\n",
    "2x+y &= 5\\\\\n",
    "x-y &= 1\n",
    "\\end{aligned}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Methods include:\n",
    "\n",
    "* [Gaussian Elimination](#Gaussian-Elimination-Method)\n",
    "* LU Decomposition\n",
    "* Jacobi Method\n",
    "* Gauss-Seidel Method\n",
    "\n",
    "Applications:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Engineering simulations\n",
    "* Machine learning\n",
    "* Data science\n",
    "\n",
    "### Interpolation\n",
    "\n",
    "Interpolation estimates unknown values between known data points.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "| x | y  |\n",
    "| - | -- |\n",
    "| 1 | 2  |\n",
    "| 2 | 5  |\n",
    "| 3 | 10 |\n",
    "\n",
    "Find the value at x=2.5\n",
    "\n",
    "Methods:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Linear Interpolation\n",
    "* Lagrange Interpolation\n",
    "* Newton Interpolation\n",
    "* Spline Interpolation\n",
    "\n",
    "### Numerical Differentiation\n",
    "\n",
    "Approximates derivatives.\n",
    "\n",
    "The derivative formula:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "f'(x)\\approx\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where h is very small.\n",
    "\n",
    "Useful when:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Function is known only through data\n",
    "* Analytical differentiation is difficult\n",
    "\n",
    "### Numerical Integration\n",
    "\n",
    "Approximates areas under curves.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\int_0^1 x^2,dx\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Exact answer:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{1}{3}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Numerical methods:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Trapezoidal Rule\n",
    "* Simpson's Rule\n",
    "* Gaussian Quadrature\n",
    "\n",
    "Applications:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Physics\n",
    "* Statistics\n",
    "* Engineering\n",
    "\n",
    "### Numerical Solutions of Differential Equations\n",
    "\n",
    "Many natural phenomena are modeled using differential equations.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{dy}{dx}=x+y\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Methods:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Euler Method\n",
    "* Runge-Kutta Methods\n",
    "* Finite Difference Methods\n",
    "\n",
    "Applications:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Population growth\n",
    "* Fluid dynamics\n",
    "* Electrical circuits\n",
    "\n",
    "## Sources of Error\n",
    "\n",
    "Errors are unavoidable because computers use finite precision.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Round-off Error\n",
    "\n",
    "Occurs because computers store only a limited number of digits.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{1}{3}=0.333333\\ldots\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Computer stores:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "0.333333\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The remaining digits are lost.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Truncation Error\n",
    "\n",
    "Occurs when an infinite process is replaced by a finite one.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "The expansion of\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "e^x\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "is\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "1+x+\\frac{x^2}{2!}+\\frac{x^3}{3!}+\\cdots\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Using only the first few terms introduces truncation error.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Measurement Error\n",
    "\n",
    "Occurs when input data itself is inaccurate.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "Length measured as:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "10.2\\pm0.1\\ \\text{cm}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The uncertainty affects the final result.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Characteristics\n",
    "\n",
    "A good numerical method should have:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Accuracy: Produces results close to the true value.\n",
    "2. Stability: Small input errors do not cause large output errors.\n",
    "3. Efficiency: Requires minimal computation time.\n",
    "4. Convergence: Approaches the exact solution as iterations increase.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Advantages\n",
    "\n",
    "* Solves problems without exact solutions\n",
    "* Handles large datasets\n",
    "* Essential for computer simulations\n",
    "* Applicable in science and engineering\n",
    "* Forms the basis of scientific computing\n",
    "\n",
    "### Limitations\n",
    "\n",
    "* Produces approximate, not exact, answers\n",
    "* Sensitive to numerical errors\n",
    "* Some methods converge slowly\n",
    "* Requires computational resources\n",
    "\n",
    "# Bisection Method\n",
    "\n",
    "The **Bisection Method** is one of the simplest and most reliable numerical methods for finding the root of a nonlinear equation.\n",
    "\n",
    "A **root** of an equation is a value of x that makes:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "f(x)=0\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The bisection method repeatedly divides an interval into two equal parts and selects the subinterval that contains the root.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Basic Idea\n",
    "\n",
    "Suppose we want to solve:\n",
    "$$\n",
    "f(x)=0\n",
    "$$\n",
    "If we can find two points a and b such that:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "f(a)\\times f(b)<0\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "then f(a) and f(b) have opposite signs.\n",
    "\n",
    "This means the graph crosses the x-axis somewhere between a and b, so at least one root exists in that interval (assuming the function is continuous).\n",
    "\n",
    "## Why It Works\n",
    "\n",
    "The method is based on the **Intermediate Value Theorem**.\n",
    "\n",
    "> If a continuous function changes sign over an interval, then it must cross zero somewhere in that interval.\n",
    "\n",
    "For example:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "f(1)=-2\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "f(2)=4\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Since the signs are different:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "(-2)(4)=-8<0\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "a root must exist between 1 and 2.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Algorithm\n",
    "\n",
    "### Choose Initial Interval\n",
    "\n",
    "Find a and b such that:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "f(a)f(b)<0\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "### Find Midpoint\n",
    "\n",
    "Use the midpoint formula:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "m=\\frac{a+b}{2}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "### Evaluate Function at Midpoint\n",
    "\n",
    "Calculate:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "f(m)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "### Select New Interval\n",
    "\n",
    "There are three possibilities:\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Case 1\n",
    "\n",
    "If\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "f(m)=0\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "then m is the root.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Case 2\n",
    "\n",
    "If\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "f(a)f(m)<0\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "the root lies between a and m.\n",
    "\n",
    "Set:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "b=m\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Case 3\n",
    "\n",
    "If\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "f(m)f(b)<0\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "the root lies between m and b.\n",
    "\n",
    "Set:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "a=m\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "### Repeat\n",
    "\n",
    "Continue until $|b-a|$ becomes very small, or the desired accuracy is achieved."
