    "The **Secant Method** is an iterative numerical technique used to find the root of a nonlinear equation. It is similar to the Newton-Raphson method, but it **does not require the derivative** $f'(x)$. Instead, it approximates the derivative using two previous points on the curve. Because it avoids derivative calculations, the Secant Method is often preferred when the derivative is difficult or expensive to compute.\n",
