    "    * If $f(x_n)=f(x_{n-1})$ the denominator becomes zero.\n",
    "\n",
    "# False Position Method\n",
    "\n",
    "The **False Position Method** (also called the **Regula Falsi Method**) is a numerical technique used to find the root of a nonlinear equation. It is a **bracketing method**, meaning it starts with two points that contain a root and repeatedly narrows the interval containing that root. The method combines the **reliability of the Bisection Method** with the idea of using a **straight-line approximation** (similar to the Secant Method).\n",
    "\n",
    "## Basic Idea\n",
    "\n",
    "Suppose we have two points:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "a \\text{ and } b\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "such that\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "f(a)f(b)<0\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "This means the function changes sign between (a) and (b), so at least one root lies in the interval. Instead of taking the midpoint (as in Bisection), the False Position Method draws a straight line (chord) connecting:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "(a,f(a))\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "and\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "(b,f(b))\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The x-coordinate where this line crosses the x-axis is taken as the next approximation to the root.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Geometric Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "Consider the graph of a continuous function.\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Choose two points a and b with opposite signs.\n",
    "2. Draw a straight line joining:\n",
    "   * (a,f(a))\n",
    "   * (b,f(b))\n",
    "3. Find where this line intersects the x-axis.\n",
    "4. Use this point as the new approximation.\n",
    "5. Keep the interval where the sign change occurs.\n",
    "6. Repeat until convergence.\n",
    "\n",
    "Because the line often intersects closer to the root than the midpoint, convergence is usually faster than Bisection.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Derivation of the Formula\n",
    "\n",
    "The equation of the line joining:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "(a,f(a))\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "and\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "(b,f(b))\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "is obtained from linear interpolation.\n",
    "\n",
    "The x-intercept is:\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x_r=\\frac{a f(b)-b f(a)}{f(b)-f(a)}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "An equivalent form often used is:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x_r=\\frac{f(a)(b-a)}\n",
    "{f(b)-f(a)}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Both formulas give the same result.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Algorithm\n",
    "\n",
    "### Step 1\n",
    "\n",
    "Choose a and b such that:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "f(a)f(b)<0\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "### Step 2\n",
    "\n",
    "Compute the approximation:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x_r=\\frac{a f(b)-b f(a)}\n",
    "{f(b)-f(a)}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "### Step 3\n",
    "\n",
    "Evaluate:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "f(x_r)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
