    "2. Solving the resulting triangular system (**back substitution**).\n",
    "\n",
    "It is one of the most fundamental algorithms in numerical analysis and serves as the basis for many advanced matrix computation techniques.\n",
    "\n",
    "# Naive Gaussian Elimination Method\n",
    "\n",
    "The **Naive Gaussian Elimination Method** is the simplest version of Gaussian Elimination used to solve a system of linear equations. It is called **\"naive\"** because it performs elimination **without any pivoting (row exchanges)**. The method assumes that all pivot elements are nonzero and sufficiently large to avoid numerical instability.\n",
