   "source": [
    "## Newton's Divided Difference Interpolation\n",
    "\n",
    "This method builds the interpolation polynomial incrementally using **divided differences**. It is especially useful when new data points are added.\n",
    "\n",
    "The interpolation polynomial is:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "P_n(x)\n",
    "=f[x_0]\n",
    "+\n",
    "f[x_0,x_1](x-x_0)\n",
    "+\n",
    "f[x_0,x_1,x_2](x-x_0)(x-x_1)\n",
    "+\\cdots\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where the coefficients are divided differences.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Divided Difference Formula\n",
    "\n",
    "First-order:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "f[x_i,x_{i+1}]\n",
    "=\\frac{f(x_{i+1})-f(x_i)}\n",
    "{x_{i+1}-x_i}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Second-order:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "f[x_i,x_{i+1},x_{i+2}]\n",
    "=\\frac{\n",
    "f[x_{i+1},x_{i+2}]\n",
    "f[x_i,x_{i+1}]\n",
    "}\n",
    "{x_{i+2}-x_i}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Given:\n",
    "\n",
    "| x | y  |\n",
    "| - | -- |\n",
    "| 1 | 1  |\n",
    "| 2 | 4  |\n",
    "| 4 | 16 |\n",
    "\n",
    "Estimate f(3).\n",
    "\n",
    "### Divided Difference Table\n",
    "\n",
    "First-order:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "f[1,2]\n",
    "=\\frac{4-1}{2-1}\n",
    "=3\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "f[2,4]\n",
    "=\\frac{16-4}{4-2}\n",
    "=6\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Second-order:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "f[1,2,4]\n",
    "=\\frac{6-3}{4-1}\n",
    "=1\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "### Construct Polynomial\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "P(x)\n",
    "=1\n",
    "+\n",
    "3(x-1)\n",
    "+\n",
    "1(x-1)(x-2)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "### Evaluate at (x=3)\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "P(3)\n",
    "=1\n",
    "+\n",
    "3(2)\n",
    "+\n",
    "(2)(1)\n",
    "=9\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "### Result\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\boxed{f(3)=9}\n",
    "$$\n"
   ]
