    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "y_i\n",
    "=\n",
    "b_i-\\sum_{j=1}^{i-1}l_{ij}y_j\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "### Back Substitution Formula\n",
    "\n",
    "For:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "UX=Y\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "the solution is:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x_i\n",
    "=\\frac{\n",
    "y_i-\\sum_{j=i+1}^{n}u_{ij}x_j\n",
    "}\n",
    "{u_{ii}}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "## Charecterstics\n",
    "\n",
    "### Advantages\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Efficient for Multiple Systems\n",
    "    * If $AX=B_1,\\quad AX=B_2,\\quad AX=B_3$ the matrix (A) is decomposed only once.\n",
    "2. Faster Than Repeated Gaussian Elimination\n",
    "    * Useful when solving many systems with the same coefficient matrix.\n",
    "3. Foundation for Advanced Numerical Methods  \n",
    "    Used in:\n",
    "    * Matrix inversion\n",
    "    * Determinants\n",
    "    * Finite element analysis\n",
    "    * Computational fluid dynamics\n",
    "    * Machine learning\n",
    "4. Computer-Friendly\n",
    "    * Widely implemented in numerical software packages.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Disadvantages\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Requires Nonsingular Matrix\n",
    "    * If $\\det(A)=0$, LU decomposition may fail.\n",
    "2. Pivoting May Be Needed\n",
    "    * Very small pivots can cause numerical instability.\n",
    "    * In practice, **LU with Partial Pivoting (PA = LU)** is commonly used.\n",
    "3. Storage Requirement\n",
    "    * Must store both (L) and (U).\n",
    "\n",
    "### Computational Complexity\n",
    "\n",
    "LU decomposition requires approximately:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{2}{3}n^3\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "operations.\n",
    "\n",
    "Complexity:\n",
    "$$\n",
    "O(n^3)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "which is similar to Gaussian Elimination.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Applications\n",
    "\n",
    "LU Decomposition is used in:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Engineering simulations\n",
    "* Structural analysis\n",
    "* Circuit analysis\n",
    "* Machine learning\n",
    "* Computer graphics\n",
    "* Numerical solutions of differential equations\n",
    "* Scientific computing\n",
    "\n",
    "### Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "The **LU Decomposition Method** factors a matrix into:\n",
    "$$\n",
    "A=LU\n",
    "$$\n",
    "where:\n",
    "\n",
    "* (L) is a lower triangular matrix.\n",
    "* (U) is an upper triangular matrix.\n",
    "\n",
    "The solution process is:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Decompose (A) into (L) and (U).\n",
    "2. Solve (LY=B) by forward substitution.\n",
    "3. Solve (UX=Y) by back substitution.\n",
    "\n",
    "For the example system\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\begin{aligned}\n",
    "2x+y-z &= 8\\\\\n",
    "-3x-y+2z &= -11\\\\\n",
    "-2x+y+2z &= -3\n",
    "\\end{aligned}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "the LU decomposition method yields:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\boxed{x=2,\\quad y=3,\\quad z=-1}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "while providing an efficient framework for solving large systems of linear equations in numerical analysis.\n"
